(M1 test C: X2Sigma+, A2Pi and B2Sigma- with different potentials, constant)
(L+ couplings and spin-rotation in X. check_m1.py contracts the saved Duo)
(eigenvectors separately with T(+1) = -(L+ + g_s S+)/sqrt(2), and compares)
(the line strengths with the Duo MAGDIPOLE output.)
masses 1.0 16.0
molecule fictitious
nstates 3
jrot 0.5 - 3.5
symmetry Cs(M)
grid
  npoints 151
  range  0.55 2.0
  type 0
end
contraction
  vib
  vmax 3 3 3
end
checkpoint
  eigenfunc save ascii
  filename M1_2Pi_2Sigma
end
poten 1
name "X2Sigma+"
type polynomial
lambda 0
mult 2
symmetry +
units cm-1
values
c0     0.0
re     0.97
c1     0.0
c2 40000.0
end
poten 2
name "A2Pi"
type polynomial
lambda 1
mult 2
units cm-1
values
c0   400.0
re     1.00
c1     0.0
c2 36000.0
end
poten 3
name "B2Sigma-"
type polynomial
lambda 0
mult 2
symmetry -
units cm-1
values
c0   900.0
re     1.03
c1     0.0
c2 33000.0
end
L+ 2 1
name "<A|L+|X>"
lambda 1 0
spin 0.5 0.5
type polynomial
values
c0 0.8
end
L+ 2 3
name "<A|L+|B>"
lambda 1 0
spin 0.5 0.5
type polynomial
values
c0 0.6
end
spin-rotation 1 1
name "<X|SR|X>"
lambda 0 0
spin 0.5 0.5
type polynomial
values
c0 0.5
end
intensity
  magdipole
  absorption
  thresh_intes 1e-300
  thresh_line 1e-300
  temperature 300
  gns 1.0 1.0
  J, 0.5, 3.5
  freq-window 0.001, 50000
  energy low -0.001, 50000, upper -0.001, 50000
end
